# Viewport interactions

The viewport reads session signals and dispatches commands. It does not edit the document.

- Convert screen, document, and object-local points only through the camera and transform helpers.
- One gesture owns one `pointerId`. Capture the pointer and release it when the gesture ends.
- A drag dispatches `gesture: 'begin'` once, then `'continue'`.
- Honor zoom limits, snap, the 4px gesture threshold, and `isInteractionLocked`.
- Keep geometry and command building in `src/app/viewport/utils/`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — screen delta written into document space
dispatch({ type: 'object.translate', ids, dx: event.movementX, dy: event.movementY, gesture: 'continue' });

// ✅ GOOD — convert with screenToDocument, then dispatch the document delta
```
